# The commits ODataKit builds on, the one place each is named: ci.yml loads
# this file (gnustep-release-actions/pins), and Docker/Dockerfile reads it.
# To move a pin, edit it here. Full commit hashes only, never branches: the
# gnustep-patches commit decides the recipe hash the stack is cached under,
# so a moving branch would keep serving a prefix built from patches that
# have since changed.

# gnustep-patches: the patched GNUstep stack (Scripts/build-gnustep.sh).
# 43dcb1f: #821 and #823 retired, merged upstream (nsxml-prefixed-
# descendants no longer applied to libs-base master, which broke every
# build from scratch); nsxml-placeholder-attributes, the rest of #821.
# Before it: NSExpression FUNCTION and FETCH for mapping-model migrations
# (0b19ede), secure predicate coding (610d60b), many fixes merged upstream.
# 7adc606 (#12), the commit every app now builds on: libs-base moved
# (#843 merged; the stack builds from scratch again), and arc4random() and
# its companions on glibc before 2.36, which the Workbench calls (its
# AppImage is built on Ubuntu 22.04, glibc 2.35).
# 60de7bc (#14): libs-base merged #847 (plist-read-binary leaves) and moved
# past it, which had stopped every build of the stack from scratch;
# libs-gui merged #984 (xib-date-picker left, #13).
GNUSTEP_PATCHES_REF=60de7bcc1ce7744581acffdc5cd3f97512af19d1

# FreeCoreData: the Core Data under the store and the server. After #74 and
# #75: a SQLite store gives back free pages after saves, and keeps a Binary
# value that allows external storage (past 128 KiB) in a file beside it, as
# Apple's does (ODataSync's synced files are so kept). Before them: object
# and context leaks fixed (#71-73), fetch indexes (#68-69), store migration
# (#63-65, #70), momc as Xcode spells a model (#40, #62, #67), shared SQL
# backends (#51, #61).
FREECOREDATA_REF=a07b87ff0cba571bbc282f99d73f37619a9f65b3
